   \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"代谢通路数据仅来自子集。F/B比率的具体生物学机制未在本研究中深入阐明。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"分析了代谢通路（如氨基酸合成、发酵）与PD-L1表达的联系，以及厚壁菌/拟杆菌比率（F/B ratio）与短PFS的联系。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::35103c949497a976bb9740b8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"观察性研究，混杂因素较多。化疗方案多样，未统一标准化。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"评估了化疗预处理对肠道菌群的影响。发现化疗确实改变了菌群组成（β-多样性差异），但这种改变并未将菌群推向特定的“不良预后”表型，且化疗预处理患者中仍保留了与PFS相关的特异性菌群差异。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d728198fecb8864ce25b1c18\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"引言中提到的“分子模拟”假说（微生物抗原与肿瘤新抗原相似，激活T细胞）以及“肠-肺轴”概念。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5098926836554035c3b06b7d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论部分指出本研究与东亚人群研究（Jin et al., Zhang et al.）结果的差异，归因于种族背景、测序方法（16S vs 宏基因组）和参考数据库的不同。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f539b66ea1f6e028c87c0c12\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究了抗生素、抗酸药（PPI）和类固醇使用对菌群的影响。发现抗酸药使用与短PFS相关菌属（链球菌）增加有关，而抗生素使用未直接关联短PFS菌属增加。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::24419f7508af418e94b98eeb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为观察性横断面研究，发现的菌群与PFS关联仅为统计学相关，不能直接推断因果关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::70e5af635ac8a33a9883b412\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"样本主要来自高加索人群，结论外推至其他种族（如亚洲、非洲）时需考虑微生物组地域差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13e15e1ea0c2a87317c8c1e9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"PFS的定义（6个月阈值）可能影响结果的解释，且未报告总生存期（OS）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::db4a1a595b125fa5470e038e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"代谢通路分析仅在部分患者中进行，可能不代表整体队列的功能特征。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7c19a38017d41f95e77105d7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机器学习模型的预测性能（AUC 0.74）属于中等水平，尚未达到临床常规应用的极高精度标准。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8ff1bcc625ac6b83f10feac7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-95bd9a77b14edf06222c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5c752c0f8036d5742e42\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a7194a689f46f19f0fc9\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5f82ba52a99d38e52a55\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5bcddf895da96806b16c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-e07b4c340a667bb2f261\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-c44cb221036f78d05573\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"missing\": [\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0001_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0001_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0002_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0002_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0003_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0003_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0004_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0004_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0005_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0005_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0006_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0006_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0007_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0007_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_SM7626.docx\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_SM7626.docx\"\n              ],\n              \"reason\": \"graphic_members_unmatched\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementary_bundle_had_no_safe_matching_images\",\n              \"status\": \"unparsed\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b67c869eee5a32d72d756c1f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::905a16b1317dae09553557fb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4fc1b23aa9738aec8d869909\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"纵向队列研究设计。收集III期黑色素瘤患者在联合ICI治疗前（基线）和治疗后第6周的配对粪便样本（n=126）和外周血PBMC样本（n=71）。使用16S rRNA基因测序分析肠道微生物组成，使用质谱流式细胞术全面 profiling 循环免疫细胞亚群。比较基线与第6周的微生物和免疫指标变化，并分析其与临床应答状态及irAEs严重程度的关联。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ddc7133862b1e98dee7bbcc4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了纵向证据，表明肠道微生物组（特别是拟杆菌属和瘤胃球菌科）与ICI治疗期间的免疫细胞动态（特别是Tregs）及临床结局（应答和irAEs）存在关联。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的统计校正方法（如多重检验校正）、微生物功能推断细节、以及是否控制了其他混杂因素（如抗生素使用、饮食等）。此外，作为会议摘要，缺乏完整的实验细节和长期随访数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5ced063ef4d895bb2527ef3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"ICI治疗前后对比\",\n          \"finding\": \"治疗导致循环中CD8+效应记忆T细胞（Tem）频率增加（P=0.0096）和调节性T细胞（Tregs）频率减少（P=0.0029）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::df0c22db80cc042e49db6078\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"根据临床应答分类\",\n          \"finding\": \"Tregs的减少主要在应答者中观察到（P=0.0016），而在非应答者中无显著变化（P=0.9515）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::155a4a53fa9c96215b2c32fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"根据irAEs严重程度分类\",\n          \"finding\": \"发生严重irAEs的患者在第6周时Tregs显著缺乏（P=0.0293），相比无或轻度毒性患者。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4dd917c890edeb09e25c7941\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基线微生物与免疫变化的关联\",\n          \"finding\": \"在循环Tregs减少的患者中，Tregs减少的程度与基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）相对丰度呈正相关（P<0.0001）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::43564e4cabb74c63d54ecf12\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基线微生物与临床结局的关联\",\n          \"finding\": \"较高的基线拟杆菌属丰度与更严重的irAEs发展（P=0.0472）及第6周前更高的类固醇使用率（P=0.0345）相关。相反，较高的瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）丰度具有保护作用，且瘤胃球菌科主导的微生物组患者中应答者比例更高。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13b30b98ec45be93bfcf01d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b52da9c89aaeaaa5b0749b6e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效，但具体机制不明。本研究试图解决：肠道微生物如何与免疫系统相互作用以影响ICI的成功或irAEs的发生？特别是特定细菌类群（如拟杆菌属和瘤胃球菌科）与免疫细胞亚群变化及临床结局之间的关联。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::15613d5b09de0b9d50378597\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"III期黑色素瘤患者，接受新辅助联合抗PD-1/抗CTLA-4免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗；涉及澳大利亚和荷兰队列（n=126），其中71名患者有匹配的PBMC数据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::35e128a47c0a17f95654887c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究旨在阐明肠道微生物组与免疫系统在ICI治疗中的纵向动态关系及其对疗效和免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。通过对126名患者的基线和第6周粪便样本进行16S rRNA基因测序，并对71名患者的外周血单个核细胞（PBMCs）进行质谱流式细胞术分析，研究发现ICI治疗导致循环中CD8+效应记忆T细胞增加和调节性T细胞（Tregs）减少。Tregs的减少主要见于应答者，但在发生严重irAEs的患者中也观察到显著缺乏。基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）丰度与Tregs减少程度及严重irAEs风险正相关，而瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）高丰度则具有保护作用并关联更好的应答。结论指出肠道微生物组可能通过影响免疫平衡的“临界点”来塑造ICI的治疗结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::46fff116fb877592fe07c91f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅针对III期黑色素瘤患者，且为新辅助联合ICI治疗情境；不能直接外推至其他肿瘤类型或单药ICI治疗。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了特定细菌类群（拟杆菌属、瘤胃球菌科）与ICI疗效（客观缓解）及毒性（irAEs严重程度）的具体关联方向和数据支持。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5ba5a4a521ab5b76c9cdd393\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这是基于观察性关联提出的假设性机制（'suggests that...'），并非经过功能验证的因果机制；需结合其他研究确认其普遍性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了一个潜在的机制线索：肠道微生物组可能通过影响基线免疫稳态（特别是Tregs的水平）来设定免疫反应的‘阈值’或‘临界点’，从而影响抗肿瘤免疫和irAEs的发生。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bed1c5a92a1c909e5a7e55ec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"摘要中提到‘how gut microbes interact with the immune system... remains unclear’，反映了该领域的知识空白和研究动机。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5fb91d23ecba19c99dc65b1b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"拟杆菌属既与Treg减少（通常关联疗效）相关，又与严重irAEs相关；而瘤胃球菌科则显示保护性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::561b8cc96f7980e0b68fb9a2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为会议摘要，详细的方法学细节（如测序深度、生物信息学流程、流式抗体面板、统计分析模型）未在摘要中提供，需谨慎引用具体数值和方法论细节。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e79b3405bb023182accfa755\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象仅限于III期黑色素瘤患者，且接受的是新辅助联合ICI治疗，结果可能不适用于晚期转移性黑色素瘤或其他实体瘤的单药ICI治疗。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fee2de282937a619aa2bdca1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"关联不等于因果：观察到的微生物与免疫细胞及临床结局的关联可能是由其他未测量的混杂因素驱动的，或反映的是反向因果关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7929958b24e5e4211328f19b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"‘拟杆菌属’是一个属水平的分类单元，其内部物种可能存在功能差异，摘要未提供更精细的分类或功能信息。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e1908b8bbd498777e918ecb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::15880bc0c9b27ea149b5f481\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69a5c41c3468c7220ec3c645\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::85fe10bf66a0ea72d4898c74\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究设计为前瞻性观察性试点研究。纳入标准：确诊为IIIA-IV期NSCLC并接受pembrolizumab（抗PD-1抗体）治疗的患者。数据采集：在治疗前获取基线粪便样本，在第一周期治疗后3周内获取第二次粪便样本。分析方法：使用QIIME v1.9.1进行16S rRNA序列分析，计算Alpha多样性（Observed, Chao1, Shannon, Simpson）和Beta多样性（Bray-Curtis dissimilarity + PERMANOVA）。使用DESeq2检测属水平上的差异丰度菌种。临床评估：基于iRECIST标准在第12周判定响应状态（CR/PR vs SD/PD）。统计比较：对比响应者与非响应者在治疗前后微生物组变化的差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::55647bb83a139b9ad1f5a1fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了小规模前瞻性数据，表明NSCLC患者在接受抗PD-1治疗期间，肠道微生物组的动态变化（而非仅基线状态）与临床响应相关。发现响应者伴随更大的微生物组多样性波动，并鉴定了特定的菌属变化模式（如响应者中Clostridium sensu stricto 1增加，无响应者中Akkermansia减少）。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量极小（N=5），仅为试点研究，不足以得出确切的因果结论或普适性规律。仅收集了一个时间点的治疗后样本，无法描绘完整的纵向轨迹。未包含所有患者（特别是无响应者）的外周血CX3CR1+ CD8+ T细胞数据，限制了微生物组与系统性免疫反应的相关性分析。化疗可能干扰微生物组，但其独立影响在本研究中未完全剥离。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c7b0afc6f541c9bb294a0bd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基线阶段，3名响应者与2名无响应者之间\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠道微生物组的整体Alpha多样性（包括Observed, Chao1, Shannon, Simpson指数）无显著差异。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c233e41e0f6c2e57947aec0a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"治疗期间，比较响应者与无响应者的微生物组变化幅度\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者表现出显著的治疗前后微生物组多样性变化（R2: 0.146, P = 0.0274），而无响应者变化较小。整体而言，治疗时间点对微生物组组成的解释力较弱（P = 0.26），个体效应较强。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c110c5934d43437de2c0d2ac\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"响应者（Responders）治疗后的特定菌属变化\",\n          \"finding\": \"Odoribacter, Gordonibacter, Candidatus Stoquefichus, Escheria-Shigella, 和 Collinsella 的丰度显著下降；Clostridium sensu stricto 1 的丰度显著增加。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6419dd7088c2e53b13242b6f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"无响应者（Non-responders）治疗后的特定菌属变化\",\n          \"finding\": \"Prevotella, Porphyromonas, Streptococcus, 和 Escheria-Shigella 的丰度显著增加；Akkermansia 的丰度显著下降。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ea9986a3cf5236e55a897e3f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::abc522398739e5d4c58fea4c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"主要问题：目前缺乏有效的非侵入性生物标志物来早期识别对PD-1/PD-L1阻断疗法有反应的NSCLC患者，且基线微生物组与疗效的关系尚不明确。具体动机：尽管已知抗生素使用影响ICI疗效，但治疗过程中肠道微生物组的组成变化及其与疗效的具体关系仍不清楚。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e2d15979eaa156c5f0e78cb3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象为接受抗PD-1免疫治疗（单药或联合化疗）的III期至IV期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者。研究情境为Roswell Park Comprehensive Cancer Center的前瞻性队列，样本量为5名患者（3名响应者，2名无响应者）。范围聚焦于治疗前及早期治疗期间粪便样本中肠道微生物组的动态变化及其与临床疗效的关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::38d2935668ccaa759a6b6432\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在探索肠道微生物组在治疗过程中的动态变化是否能作为预测非小细胞肺癌患者对PD-1抑制剂反应的非侵入性生物标志物。鉴于基线微生物组特征和肿瘤组织PD-L1表达的预测价值有限，作者分析了5名患者的配对粪便样本，通过16S rRNA测序比较响应者与无响应者在治疗前后的微生物多样性及组成差异。研究发现，虽然基线α多样性在两组间无显著差异，但响应者在治疗期间的微生物多样性发生了显著改变，而无响应者则相对稳定或呈现不同的菌群演变模式。这表明治疗期间的微生物组波动可能与免疫治疗的疗效相关。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::60bb2b4a9aa9df9db01788b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限NSCLC人群，样本量小（N=5），且混合了单药与联合化疗方案，结果的外推需谨慎。不能证明因果关系，仅为关联观察。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了具体的临床观察证据：在NSCLC患者中，治疗期间肠道微生物组的显著变化（波动）与抗PD-1治疗的响应正相关，而稳定的或特定菌属（如Akkermansia减少）的变化与无响应相关。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e83c2e1bd28e65ccf7087396\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这是相关性发现，未提供直接的机制验证（如代谢产物分析或动物模型验证）。所给材料未交代这些菌属变化的具体分子机制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提示了潜在的机制线索：响应者中Clostridium sensu stricto 1的增加和无响应者中Akkermansia的减少可能与免疫激活或抑制有关。同时指出Escheria-Shigella在无响应者中的增加与既往文献一致。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eab5db6ff6e6bd9baf462ffc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文引言讨论了基线微生物组、抗生素使用、粪菌移植（FMT）与ICI疗效的关系，以及当前基线生物标志物（如PD-L1）的局限性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7d78b42fa14a1be3044aa718\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"使用了16S rRNA测序（V3-V4区）和标准的生物信息学流程（QIIME, DESeq2）来分析配对样本。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1bd3e81cd7e640495cb12068\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"样本量极小（N=5），结果可能存在过拟合或偶然性，不能代表总体人群。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::246effc5bffc4f5957f9d1d4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究纳入了联合化疗患者，化疗本身对微生物组的影响未被单独控制，可能导致混杂。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cbe5d95acd9ad45b5d33eee2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"仅有一个治疗时间点样本，无法区分短期波动与长期趋势。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0b5f55cb4a345f60d7fb9eb6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者声称的“潜在用途”需结合其他更大规模研究综合评估，不可单独视为确证证据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5a6c058a106fbb14db28ef44\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-95bd9a77b14edf06222c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5c752c0f8036d5742e42\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a7194a689f46f19f0fc9\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2e6d4dfc0cdc627820931355\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c68801c53064238d6315c89\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4cbcd1bdd69fde55c51229cf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 纵向数据采集：对92名接受pembrolizumab治疗的晚期NSCLC患者进行串行样本采集。2. 多组学分析：对患者样本进行肠道微生物组测序、RNA-seq和WES分析。3. 对照比较：将患者微生物数据与92名健康对照进行比较，分析免疫治疗期间的微生物特征变化。4. 队列整合与验证：结合内部队列与728例公开ICI治疗队列数据，开发用于分类ICI反应的评分。5. 评分优化：基于响应者与非响应者相关微生物标记物的比率构建跨人群评分，并与TMB联合评估其分层能力。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9234bfeff0816e566ab0c7f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了纵向多组学证据，明确了特定菌群（Faecalibacterium vs Lactobacillus/Escherichia）与NSCLC患者ICI疗效的关联，并揭示了微生物失调随治疗和进展的动态轨迹。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的统计模型细节、多组学数据整合的具体算法、以及TMB联合评分在不同亚组中的具体性能指标（如AUC值）。此外，相关性不等于因果性，饮食和抗生素的影响需进一步控制混杂因素验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f5f3ff45c44d58bc524af1f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在92名NSCLC患者队列中，根据RECIST标准定义的反应者（CR/PR或SD≥6个月）与非反应者对比\",\n          \"finding\": \"反应者富集Faecalibacterium属，非反应者富集Lactobacillus和Escherichia属；这些菌群的丰度与膳食纤维摄入和抗生素使用存在特定关联。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f962de69aff3170c50d46d9f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"纵向观察治疗期间及疾病进展时的微生物失调动态\",\n          \"finding\": \"在治疗后，仅反应者的微生物特征与健康队列的差异性降低；而在疾病进展时，无论反应者还是非反应者，其与正常队列的差异性均增加。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dbab987f2615c8ecf70dc648\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"利用内部队列和728例公共ICI队列数据开发的跨人群评分\",\n          \"finding\": \"该评分基于响应者/非响应者相关微生物标记物比率，与反映肠道微生物健康状态的指数呈显著正相关；当与肿瘤突变负荷（TMB）结合时，提高了ICI疗效的分层准确性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d75c5834eaf3870ae01a1445\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f891faea0d8fe7e53741a5ed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组与ICI反应有关，但缺乏纵向多组学研究来明确具体因素及其动态变化机制。本研究旨在识别导致治疗反应差异的具体微生物和宿主因素，并开发一种能够跨人群验证的疗效预测评分。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9fc32fab0a091de0eb039d21\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象为接受帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）治疗的晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者。研究情境包括内部队列（92名患者，进行纵向多组学分析）、健康对照队列（92人）以及外部公共ICI治疗队列（728人）。范围涵盖肠道微生物组、宿主转录组（RNA-seq）和全外显子组测序（WES），旨在识别影响免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的因素。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::be7f277a94f66204fd567864\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究针对肠道微生物组与ICI疗效关联中纵向多组学数据不足的现状，对92例晚期NSCLC患者进行了纵向采样和多组学分析。通过比较患者与健康人的微生物特征，并利用内部队列及728例公共数据开发并验证了一个分类评分系统。研究发现特定菌群丰度与治疗反应相关，观察到治疗过程中微生物失调的动态变化，并提出了一个结合肿瘤突变负荷（TMB）的跨人群评分以改善疗效分层。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c75ab0a7f525c3cdcfd56bcf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"结论基于NSCLC患者队列，虽结合了公共ICI数据，但主要发现仍局限于肺癌语境下的微生物特征；评分的有效性依赖于特定的标记物选择和健康状态指数。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了具体的微生物分类群（Faecalibacterium, Lactobacillus, Escherichia）与ICI疗效（CR/PR/SD vs PD）的关联证据，并开发了基于这些标记物比率的跨人群评分。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::697fab1e944be79f63331cce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"摘要未提供具体的分子机制（如代谢产物、免疫细胞浸润等），仅描述了表型层面的动态变化和统计学关联；无法直接解释因果机制，仅能作为机制研究的背景或假设生成依据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了微生物失调的动态变化模式：反应者治疗后向健康状态回归，而进展期所有患者均出现恶化。同时指出微生物特征与TMB具有互补性。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::26c8e9ef23383e9bd70bc9a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究发现特定菌群与膳食纤维摄入和抗生素使用有关联。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::91f6c9b443b00edda18f6269\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"微生物评分与TMB结合提高了分层准确性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cf589dd5bc8c56c8193ab89d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为观察性纵向研究，发现的菌群与疗效关联为相关性，不能直接推断因果关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::606f3a3f6e5e9b33a1fb74d1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"微生物特征的动态变化（如治疗后向健康状态回归）仅在反应者中观察到，非反应者在进展期恶化，这一模式需谨慎外推至其他肿瘤类型或治疗线数。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8420884f93801885a20acf8b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"评分系统的开发使用了公共数据，但其具体权重和阈值未在摘要中披露，使用时需注意可重复性限制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3147586d331aea68e8905ba3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"所给材料未提供详细的统计显著性数值（如P值、置信区间），仅定性描述“显著正相关”。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a4238167e6163f4ef5f1f19a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"html\",\n              \"reason\": \"html_not_scholarly_body\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_plus_snippets\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fe8dbe80e1b345cf463a700c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::63d6761df76fcc28abb72d65\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::799dc90a7500725ba934e5e4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"A prospective observational cohort design was used. Clinical data for 74 patients were analyzed for associations between antibiotic/probiotic use and survival outcomes (PFS, OS, ORR) using Kaplan-Meier analysis and Cox regression. For 18 patients with complete dynamic sampling, metagenomic sequencing and untargeted metabolomics were performed. Microbial alpha/beta diversity, differential taxa abundance, and dynamic trajectory types (U-shaped vs. inverted U-shaped) were analyzed. Metabolite differences between responders and non-responders were identified via UHPLC-MS, followed by correlation analysis between specific microbial taxa and metabolites.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::21b032f497e11ad82f077478\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides the first multi-omics characterization of gut microbiota and metabolites in EGFR+ NSCLC patients undergoing ICI therapy, identifying distinct microbial and metabolic signatures different from those reported in EGFR- NSCLC.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Single-center study with a small sample size for omics analysis (n=18). Observational design limits causal inference. The lack of Akkermansia muciniphila as a predictor suggests population-specific or subtype-specific differences that require validation in larger cohorts.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f31eb3ef8495f0907f8d0857\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Advanced EGFR+ NSCLC patients treated with ICIs\",\n          \"finding\": \"Antibiotic use (within 2 months before/after ICI initiation) was significantly associated with shorter progression-free survival (mPFS 4.8 vs. 6.7 months; HR 3.18) and overall survival. Probiotic use had no significant impact on PFS or OS.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b00cd4addabe5f051094b7ec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Comparison of responders vs. non-responders based on metagenomic sequencing\",\n          \"finding\": \"No significant difference in baseline alpha or beta diversity. Responders were enriched in Bradyrhizobium guangdongense, Plantactinospora sp., Corynebacterium stationis, and Methanococcus vannielii. Non-responders were enriched in Nocardioides sp., Candidatus thioglobus sp., Burkholderia anthina, and Brachybacterium sp. Notably, known beneficial species like Akkermansia muciniphila were not found to be predictive in this cohort.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2321908271fcad576e47dcec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Dynamic changes in gut microbiota over time (Baseline -> Response -> Progression)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Two dynamic patterns were identified in the 18 longitudinally sampled patients: 'U-type' (abundance decreased at response, increased at progression, e.g., Enterococcus gallinarum) and 'Inverted U-type' (abundance increased at response, decreased at progression, e.g., Mycobacterium paragordonae).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2d378659198997c365edf5df\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Metabolomic profiling of responders vs. non-responders\",\n          \"finding\": \"Responders showed enrichment of deoxycholic acid, glycerol, and quinolinic acid. Non-responders showed enrichment of L-citrulline. Significant correlations were observed between specific microbial taxa and these metabolites.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::399aa4789f191d531f10450c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5e7e721cb1761802b4554575\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The effects of gut microbiota and metabolites on ICI responses have been well-studied in EGFR wild-type (EGFR-) NSCLC, but remain unknown in EGFR-mutated (EGFR+) NSCLC. Given that EGFR+ tumors are often immunologically cold and show limited benefit from ICIs compared to EGFR- tumors, there is a need to elucidate whether gut microbiota characteristics can predict or influence ICI efficacy in this distinct molecular subtype.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::72b8df7aef468dc5c563524b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Advanced EGFR-mutated (EGFR+) non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) after resistance to EGFR-tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs). The study focuses on the association between clinical factors (antibiotic/probiotic use), gut microbiota composition and dynamics, fecal metabolites, and immunotherapy efficacy.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e71a1eb72eede5f1828bbca1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This prospective cohort study investigated the impact of gut microbiota and metabolites on the efficacy of ICIs in a specific subgroup of NSCLC patients with EGFR mutations. The research enrolled 74 advanced EGFR+ NSCLC patients and collected detailed clinical data regarding antibiotic and probiotic usage. Fecal samples were dynamically collected from 18 patients at four time points: baseline, early on-treatment, response, and progression. Metagenomic next-generation sequencing and ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry (UHPLC-MS) were employed to analyze microbial composition and metabolic profiles. The study aimed to identify biomarkers and mechanisms linking the gut environment to ICI outcomes in this population, which is often considered immunologically 'cold'.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ccbb8d260cff2b9ce6c84e79\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Limited to EGFR+ NSCLC; does not establish causality for probiotic neutrality.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies that antibiotic use significantly worsens PFS in EGFR+ NSCLC patients on ICIs, while probiotics have no effect. This contrasts with some studies in other cancers or EGFR- NSCLC where probiotics might show benefit, highlighting the complexity of microbiome interventions.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e1e88637ee445522384bfa4e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Based on a small omics cohort (n=18); requires validation.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Discovers specific microbial taxa associated with response in EGFR+ NSCLC (Bradyrhizobium guangdongense, etc.) that differ from the canonical markers (e.g., Akkermansia) found in EGFR- NSCLC.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b3702a3197e89eed1f4c5e8f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Correlational only; in vivo/in vitro validation is needed as stated by authors.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Links specific metabolites (deoxycholic acid, glycerol, quinolinic acid in responders; L-citrulline in non-responders) to microbial taxa and clinical response. Suggests metabolic pathways like tryptophan metabolism and lipolysis regulation as potential mediators.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::08db0dba8af6563011c2fd5f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion notes that EGFR+ tumors are immunologically cold and that baseline diversity did not differ between responders/non-responders, unlike in some EGFR- studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d63c43f8d3cba44a960ee6a2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Identification of 'U-type' and 'Inverted U-type' dynamic trajectories of microbial abundance relative to treatment response and progression.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2581070271d137c95ba7e99f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Findings are specific to EGFR-mutated NSCLC; results cannot be directly extrapolated to EGFR-wild type or other solid tumors without caution.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0aec56d0c003ddcdfad97f7a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The omics analysis is based on a small subset (18 patients) of the total cohort (74 patients); statistical power for microbial/metabolic associations is limited.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b64e2f1e48a78dcdb499a56f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The study is observational; associations between antibiotics/microbiota and outcomes do not prove causation.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf640c1bebb2844ced09d6be\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Probiotic neutrality should not be interpreted as proof of ineffectiveness in all contexts, but rather as an observation in this specific cohort with potentially varying probiotic formulations/durations.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ed527d6672ea83dc3ced6b92\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::43292a8e25697a7a2b821c6a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::05c6ea6e669a12d87d90425b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::31cba66826bdd392741dbc24\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究设计为前瞻性观察性队列研究。收集27例黑色素瘤患者治疗前粪便样本，分别进行16S rRNA基因测序（V4区）和鸟枪法宏基因组测序。其中17例样本因RNA质量合格进一步进行宏转录组测序。统计分析方面，使用Cox比例风险模型调整协变量（年龄、性别、BMI、分期等），评估α多样性、β多样性聚类及特定分类单元/功能通路与PFS的关联。采用500次×10折交叉验证的弹性网络惩罚Cox回归筛选显著相关的特征。宏转录组部分，计算基因家族、反应和通路的相对表达量，并与宏基因组丰度进行Spearman相关性分析，以确认功能的转录活性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ee7c7106cfc2e786d4d2e4a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了在人类黑色素瘤患者中，肠道微生物组成、特定物种及宏基因组功能通路（含转录表达）与免疫治疗无进展生存期关联的证据；首次在同一研究中整合宏基因组与宏转录组数据以关联临床预后。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量较小（n=27，宏转录组n=17）；未能单独分析辅助治疗与转移性患者亚组，也未能按免疫治疗类型（单药vs联合）分层分析；宏转录组分析因样本量限制统计效力不足；结果可能存在队列特异性，需更大规模研究验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::24acf74201156137d9b43346\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"27例黑色素瘤患者，调整协变量后\",\n          \"finding\": \"较高的微生物群落丰富度（16S s-OTU数和鸟枪法子物种数）与较长的无进展生存期（PFS）显著相关（p < 0.05）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b0b1a04089a4113806fc84ec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基于JSD距离的Ward层次聚类，区分高、中、低风险组\",\n          \"finding\": \"低风险组（富集F. prausnitzii等）相比高风险组（富集Bacteroides spp.）在任何随访时间点具有99%更低的进展风险（HR=0.01, p=0.002）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ec8e3d930bc2c3e508c94a15\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"500×10折交叉验证弹性网络Cox回归筛选\",\n          \"finding\": \"与较短PFS相关的物种包括：Bacteroides ovatus, Bacteroides dorei, Bacteroides massiliensis, Ruminococcus gnavus, Blautia producta；与较长PFS相关的物种包括：Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Coprococcus eutactus, Prevotella stercorea, Streptococcus sanguinis, Streptococcus anginosus, Lachnospiraceae bacterium 3 1 46FAA。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8be25514637782d7f88627e5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"宏基因组与宏转录组联合分析（n=17子集）\",\n          \"finding\": \"识别出与PFS相关且具有显著转录表达的宏基因组通路：风险相关通路包括L-鼠李糖降解、鸟苷核苷酸生物合成、B族维生素（泛酸、吡哆醛-5-磷酸、黄素、叶酸前体）生物合成；保护相关通路包括L-异亮氨酸生物合成。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9e353b4848cda9d7ba50ea4c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0aeee4fa349ad6804e7718af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"既往关于肠道微生物影响免疫治疗的研究结果不一致，且多数仅关注物种丰度而未考虑功能表达，也未充分利用时间-事件数据（常二分化患者为响应者/非响应者）。本研究试图通过整合16S、宏基因组和宏转录组数据，更精确地鉴定与无进展生存期相关的特定微生物类群和功能通路，并探索其潜在的机制联系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::29a4f46df8425be012292ee7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"27例接受免疫治疗（抗PD-1或抗CTLA-4）的转移性或辅助性黑色素瘤患者；研究基于治疗前粪便样本，采用16S rRNA基因测序、鸟枪法宏基因组测序及子集（n=17）的宏转录组测序；主要终点为无进展生存期（PFS）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9a77bfdf071594bc0086aebd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在探究肠道微生物群对黑色素瘤免疫治疗疗效的影响。通过对27名患者的治疗前粪便样本进行多组学分析，研究发现较高的微生物群落丰富度与较长的无进展生存期相关。基于整体微生物组成的聚类分析将患者分为高、中、低风险组，其中低风险组的疾病进展风险显著低于高风险组。在物种层面，拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）中的部分菌种（如B. ovatus, B. dorei）与较短的PFS相关，而粪杆菌属（Faecalibacterium）中的F. prausnitzii等则与较长的PFS相关。此外，研究首次结合宏转录组数据，识别出与PFS相关的宏基因组功能通路及其转录表达，包括L-鼠李糖降解、鸟苷核苷酸生物合成和B族维生素生物合成等风险相关通路，以及异亮氨酸生物合成等保护相关通路。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::00b11793deff66a1d919563f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限黑色素瘤患者；样本量小；未区分不同免疫药物类型的差异；关联而非因果。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物组成（丰富度、聚类分组）和特定物种丰度与免疫治疗疗效（PFS）正负向关联的具体数据。证实了较高丰富度和特定保护性菌种（如F. prausnitzii）与更好预后相关，而特定风险菌种（如B. ovatus）与较差预后相关。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::871f50f4dcbe93707acc51ed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制仅为推测，基于相关性分析；宏转录组样本量有限（n=17），统计效力不足；无法直接证明这些通路在体内确实导致了免疫调节；所给摘要未交代具体的代谢物浓度测量或动物实验验证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了潜在的机制线索：识别出与PFS相关的宏基因组功能通路及其转录表达。具体包括：风险通路（L-鼠李糖降解、鸟苷核苷酸合成、B族维生素合成）和保护通路（L-异亮氨酸合成）。作者推测这些代谢产物可能通过影响T细胞功能或肿瘤微环境来调节疗效。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ff44063c2bde32931bb20b1a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文讨论了既往研究（Gopalakrishnan et al., Matson et al.等）在物种发现上的不一致性，并指出功能冗余可能是关键决定因素的观点。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::345c79f514e73c54a4e5a1ce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"使用了16S、宏基因组和宏转录组的多组学整合策略，以及500×10折交叉验证的弹性网络Cox回归进行特征选择。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eb725823ea2bd9cc8e0f9c70\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究仅在黑色素瘤中进行，结论不能直接外推至其他固体肿瘤，尽管综述主题包含所有固体肿瘤。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a49e41e5085e72c62aeb151e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"宏转录组数据仅来自17名患者，因此关于转录表达与预后的关联应被视为初步探索性结果，统计效力受限。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f7fc3caa6b68a944e1d98686\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者提出的机制（如代谢物影响T细胞）是基于文献引用的推测，并非本研究的直接实验证据，需在综述中明确区分观察到的关联与提出的假设。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d46959426cc7755d82f0e7f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"未区分辅助治疗与转移性患者，也未按免疫治疗类型分层，因此无法判断微生物效应是否受治疗阶段或药物类型调节。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e152719a4ba4f5b110b4a7c6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7de762c194aeb4f84f1e\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::025edc534ec6facc5918e970\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ecf117da6fb0ce8cf42daec5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4ec8717ea1fb9c13cffbce1b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"前瞻性队列设计：连续纳入MD Anderson的MM患者。样本采集包括：(1) 粪便标本（全宏基因组鸟枪法测序WMS、微生物组分析及16S rRNA基因测序）；(2) 黏膜表面拭子（WMS测序）；(3) FFPE肿瘤标本（Bruker数字空间 profiling DSP）；(4) 新鲜肿瘤样本（正常和肿瘤组织的WES/WGS、RNA测序、T细胞受体测序）。分析重点在于比较不同原发部位微生物特征的异质性、肿瘤突变负荷（TMB）及突变签名，并对比ICI治疗响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）的微生物组成差异及DSP免疫标记物表达水平。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a63e039ca90b3c9c6ce663cd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了黏膜黑色素瘤不同原发部位（口鼻、泌尿生殖、直肠等）的特异性微生物组和基因组特征基线数据；初步揭示了ICI响应者与响应者在肠道菌群组成及肿瘤微环境免疫标记物（CD56, CD20）上的关联。\",\n          \"limits\": \"研究仍在进行中，仅报告了部分入组患者的初步分析结果，缺乏完整的长期随访疗效数据；样本量相对较小（n=130，其中完成微生物组测序85人）；未提供具体的因果机制验证，仅为相关性观察；摘要未交代统计分析的具体细节及多重比较校正方法。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bc1422b9fae5b64d5014930b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基于截至2026年5月入组的130名患者（已测序粪便和黏膜拭子85人），按原发部位分类。\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠道和黏膜表面微生物组显示出广泛的样本内异质性，且微生物特征与原发部位相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3fad70e7d4cee75ed5a89c85\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基于WES和WGS数据分析。\",\n          \"finding\": \"肿瘤突变负荷（TMB）中位数为1.34 mut/Mb（范围0.52–14.72）。直肠和泌尿生殖道肿瘤与DNA错配修复和微卫星不稳定性相关的突变签名有关；结膜和口鼻肿瘤与紫外线暴露相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::26a92b9bc963407db444dccb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"针对接受ICI治疗的患者的肠道微生物组分析。\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）之间细菌类群的存在和比例存在组成差异。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c9fa6ec476c115cb9276312c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"DSP分析按治疗反应分组。\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者（R）的免疫和肿瘤区室中CD56和CD20的表达高于非响应者。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ef634aa1dff03d968764acf4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::891c061f6e1b35c8496600b9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"黏膜黑色素瘤是一种罕见亚型，对ICI反应率低。本研究试图确定肠道、黏膜和肿瘤微生物组以及可改变的风险因素如何影响ICI的响应和耐药，特别是通过解析微生物组与肿瘤微环境的相互作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::99d5bdcfbf4a118d8408c980\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"黏膜黑色素瘤（MM）患者队列，涉及肠道、黏膜表面及肿瘤微环境的微生物组与宿主免疫/基因组互作；研究情境为前瞻性观察性研究，数据截至2026年5月。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::938112d9bf702269316f1024\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究旨在阐明微生物组与肿瘤微环境相互作用如何驱动黏膜黑色素瘤对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的响应与耐药。研究在MD安德森癌症中心前瞻性纳入MM患者，收集粪便、黏膜拭子及肿瘤组织样本进行多组学分析。初步结果显示，不同原发部位的MM具有特定的微生物特征和突变谱；在接受ICI治疗的患者中，响应者与非响应者在肠道菌群组成上存在差异，且响应者肿瘤微环境中CD56和CD20表达更高。这是一项正在进行中的研究，目前提供了部分基线数据和初步关联结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3caf73fb053b6436a58289fd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限黏膜黑色素瘤亚型；结果为初步相关性，尚未确立因果性或普适性；样本量有限。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了黏膜黑色素瘤患者中，ICI响应者与非响应者之间肠道微生物组组成的具体差异证据（细菌类群存在和比例的变化）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::174dac331c10482c9b499eeb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"CD56/CD20表达与微生物组之间的直接因果联系未在摘要中证实，仅为并行观察到的现象；机制解释尚不明确，需进一步实验验证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提示了微生物组可能与肿瘤微环境免疫状态相关联，表现为响应者中CD56和CD20表达升高。同时指出了不同原发部位MM具有不同的突变签名（如MMR缺陷 vs UV损伤），这可能间接影响免疫原性和微生物组互作。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b2f4a369c8011c98960b26ff\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"不同原发部位（口鼻、泌尿生殖、直肠、结膜）MM具有独特的微生物特征和基因组突变签名（如UV暴露相关 vs MMR缺陷相关）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::32396aee7cbda217c69e93a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"MM整体对ICI反应率低，且本研究正在探索可改变的风险因素。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1ccc88cdddfbf0f6f604fa46\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为进行中中的前瞻性队列，数据截至2026年5月，结果仅为初步分析，不代表最终结论。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7252567914c781709c40c1f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"微生物组与ICI响应的关联仅为观察性相关性，未证明因果关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3414ff342a8a474b3279096c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"样本量较小（n=130），且仅部分患者完成了微生物组测序，可能存在选择偏倚。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::11978337d32cb53b592725f8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"不同原发部位的生物学差异巨大，结果不可直接外推至其他类型的黑色素瘤或实体瘤。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::be82f4a21379d0105e536ace\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"CD56和CD20的高表达是响应者的特征，但其与微生物组的具体互作机制未知。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e412dc26845f73c0fdf22063\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a99646db3b749ddfd25fe40\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::deb5f1b5a0ec5f896f857444\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::08554aa4c222491df9d38ef8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Single-arm, multicenter phase I clinical trial. Patients received bowel preparation, followed by oral administration of capsules containing stool from one of three healthy male donors. Anti-PD1 therapy (nivolumab or pembrolizumab) started at least 7 days post-FMT. Outcomes were assessed using RECIST 1.1 criteria. Survival analysis used Kaplan-Meier methods. Metagenomic sequencing was performed on stool samples to analyze taxonomic composition (MetaPhlAn) and functional gene families (HUMAnN). Post hoc subgroup analyses compared responders vs. non-responders and patients with vs. without FMT-specific toxicity (FT) based on microbial and functional profiles.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::37fd84d50ba8233eb66b5714\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides long-term survival data (median OS 52.8 months) for a small cohort of advanced melanoma patients treated with oral FMT plus anti-PD1, demonstrating high safety and promising efficacy signals compared to historical controls.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Small sample size (N=20), single-arm design without a control group, and lack of statistical power for definitive conclusions. Results are hypothesis-generating. Patient selection bias (excluded those appropriate for combination therapy).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b7e3e6165a31ec1e105e75b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies potential biomarkers for response, linking FMT-specific mild toxicity and long-term survival to specific microbial taxa (e.g., SCFA producers) and functional metabolic pathways (glycan modification, SCFA biosynthesis).\",\n          \"limits\": \"Associations are derived from post hoc analyses. Causality between specific microbes/enzymes and clinical benefit is not established. The 'donor effect' could not be clearly disentangled due to the small cohort and mixed donor usage.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::024518a823f6006dd3e972f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Entire cohort (N=20), median follow-up 52.8 months\",\n          \"finding\": \"Median PFS was 29.6 months; median OS was 52.8 months. ORR was 65% (4 complete responses). Safety profile showed no increase in severe immune-related adverse events (irAEs); only grade 3 toxicities occurred.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3485959e4adbd9d7481e46dc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Responders (R, N=13) vs. Non-responders (NR, N=7)\",\n          \"finding\": \"R patients had significantly longer mPFS (52.8 vs. 5.2 months, p=0.0016) and longer mOS (52.8 vs. 17.6 months, p=0.0628). R patients sustained donor-derived microbial similarity over time.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7ebb834ea4cc8b7658e4ac8d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Patients with FMT-specific toxicity (FT, N=8) vs. Without FT (NFT, N=12)\",\n          \"finding\": \"All 8 FT patients were responders. FT patients had significantly improved mPFS (52.8 vs. 15.9 months, p=0.0364) and trend towards improved mOS (53.9 vs. 24.6 months, p=0.0610). FT was associated with enrichment of SCFA-producing taxa and glycan-modifying enzymes.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dffaafcf80cafef8980d6a54\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Long-term survivors (LTS) vs. Short-term survivors (STS)\",\n          \"finding\": \"LTS were enriched for commensal bacteria (Alistipes, Faecalibacterium) and enzymes involved in amino acid/SCFA biosynthesis. STS were enriched for stress-associated oxidative metabolism pathways and Hungatella hathewayi.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a938bbf69ccdde1dcf569c84\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::19f5ba98faa7f71a33a18835\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To evaluate whether modifying the gut microbiome via oral FMT from healthy donors can improve the safety, response rate, and survival outcomes of anti-PD1 therapy in patients with advanced melanoma who are naive to advanced-stage treatment, potentially overcoming primary resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f99b8e9719b07fd9b3d34bf5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Advanced cutaneous melanoma patients (N=20), treatment-naïve for advanced disease, receiving oral fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) from healthy donors followed by single-agent anti-PD1 therapy. Multicenter phase I trial conducted in Canada.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::835431f5f287a104ceabd51e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This study reports the final survival outcomes of the MIMic phase I trial, evaluating the safety and efficacy of combining oral FMT with healthy donor stool and anti-PD1 immunotherapy as first-line treatment for advanced melanoma. The trial enrolled 20 patients who received a single dose of FMT followed by nivolumab or pembrolizumab. The primary endpoint was safety, while secondary endpoints included objective response rate (ORR), progression-free survival (PFS), and overall survival (OS). The study found that the combination was safe, with an ORR of 65%. Median PFS was 29.6 months and median OS was 52.8 months, figures reported as higher than historical randomized controlled trials (RCTs) and real-world data. Post hoc analyses linked clinical responses to specific microbial engraftment patterns and functional metabolic pathways, suggesting that successful microbiome modulation may enhance ICI efficacy.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f8959cd8dd927a10f9dd3654\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Results are from a single-arm, small-sample Phase I trial. Cannot establish causal superiority over standard care due to lack of concurrent control arm. Patient population was restricted to those unsuitable for combination immunotherapy.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Reports clinical efficacy outcomes (ORR 65%, mPFS 29.6 mo, mOS 52.8 mo) for FMT+anti-PD1 in advanced melanoma, showing improvements over historical RCT benchmarks for anti-PD1 alone.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::da8e241ae0ffdf09b558a4ff\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Mechanisms are inferred from correlative post hoc analyses. The role of FMT-specific toxicity as a proxy for engraftment success is observational. Functional profiling relies on metagenomic prediction, which may not reflect actual protein activity or host interaction.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Links clinical response to specific microbial features: Responders and long-term survivors show enrichment of SCFA-producing taxa (Blautia, Roseburia, Faecalibacterium) and enzymes for glycan modification/amino acid biosynthesis. Non-responders/short-term survivors show enrichment of oxidative/stress pathways and Hungatella hathewayi.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d1f3aa72134d1a09a615318\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Comparison of oral capsule-based FMT (this study) vs. invasive colonoscopic FMT (referenced in intro). This study supports the feasibility and safety of oral delivery for systemic immune modulation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::76bf45b8fc5ee9800416db98\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"No increase in severe irAEs; FMT-specific toxicities were mild (Grade 1-2 GI).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fb82a0f9f419547426bb1f12\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Acknowledges small sample size, lack of control arm, and hypothesis-generating nature of results.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::754021e869ff2a2dba53a7aa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The study population is limited to advanced cutaneous melanoma patients ineligible for combination immunotherapy; results may not generalize to other solid tumors or earlier-stage disease.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a37fb175d8428498e2cdd297\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Survival comparisons with historical RCTs are noted by authors but are confounded by patient selection biases and temporal changes in care; do not treat as definitive proof of superiority.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de45d8ce55cd7c245f96e6fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Microbial associations are correlational; causality between specific taxa/pathways and ICI response is not proven within this study design.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::faf64be5a80ca4ce1d2dbf3a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"paper_title\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::004e7d4bb46dac64f072d7f4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"plain_text\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e055ed851f0bbe3c6e1076f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为20名晚期黑色素瘤患者；供体为3名健康男性；给药方式为口服胶囊；预处理为PEG肠道准备；无抗生素使用。\",\n              \"finding\": \"MIMic试验使用了来自三位健康男性供体的粪便进行口服FMT。所有患者均接受单一供体的粪便（每位患者对应一位供体），未混合多供体粪便。供体经过“严格的选择标准”筛选（文中引用了之前的出版物Craven et al. 2017及Routy et al. 2023中的详细标准）。FMT产品以胶囊形式给药，每剂包含35-40粒胶囊，相当于80-100克粪便。在给予FMT前一天，患者使用聚乙二醇（PEG）基肠道准备液进行预处理，且治疗期间未使用抗生素。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R12\",\n                \"R13\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为FMT干预标准化中供体筛选和制备流程的具体案例，展示如何通过严格筛选和健康供体来源来保证干预的一致性和安全性，同时指出单供体使用的局限性。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"MIMic试验在供体筛选和FMT制备方面采取了高度标准化的策略，旨在确保干预的安全性和微生物定植的可预测性。\\n\\n1. **供体筛选标准**：研究采用了“严格的选择标准”（stringent selection criteria）来筛选健康供体。虽然正文未列出具体排除指标的细节，但明确引用了关于代谢综合征疾病FMT供体筛选成本的研究（Craven et al., 2017, R13）以及该团队之前发表的I期试验方案（Routy et al., 2023, R12），暗示其遵循了当时临床前或早期临床试验中较为严格的卫生学、传染病及健康状况筛查流程。这种严格筛选是作为正面教材的，因为它最大限度地降低了传播病原体或引入致病微生物的风险，确保了“健康供体粪便”这一干预物的纯净度。\\n\\n2. **FMT制备与给药流程**：\\n   - **单一供源 vs 混合供源**：试验设计采用单一供体粪便（single healthy donor stool），每位患者仅接受来自三位指定男性供体中某一人的粪便。这种做法简化了批次管理，减少了不同供体间微生物组异质性带来的混杂因素，有利于评估特定微生物组合对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）的反应。然而，这也可能是一个反面教材或局限性，因为缺乏多供体混合可能无法覆盖更广泛的有益菌群多样性，且文中提到“没有明显的供体效应”，说明单个供体的效果在不同患者间可能存在差异，但未深入探讨混合供体是否会更优。\\n   - **制剂形式**：将粪便制成口服胶囊（35-40粒/剂，含80-100g粪便），而非传统的灌肠或鼻胃管给药。这提高了患者的依从性，减少了侵入性操作带来的感染风险，是FMT非侵入化、标准化的重要进展。\\n   - **预处理与辅助措施**：在FMT前一日使用PEG基肠道准备液，旨在清除原有肠道内容物，为新菌群定植腾出生态位。特别值得注意的是，研究中明确禁止使用抗生素，以避免抗生素对肠道菌群的破坏干扰FMT的效果或引起耐药性问题。这种“清洁但不杀菌”的准备策略是标准化流程中的关键控制点。\\n\\n总体而言，该试验通过严格的供体准入、单一的供体来源、标准化的胶囊制剂以及特定的肠道预处理，构建了一套可重复的FMT干预流程。其成功的关键在于确保了输入菌群的健康属性和定植潜力，为后续观察微生物组变化与临床疗效的关系提供了可靠的基础。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"文中引用的供体筛选具体指标（如具体的病原体检测列表、BMI限制、饮食要求等）未在本文正文中详细列出，需参考R12和R13获取完整细节。\",\n            \"单一供体与多供体混合在长期定植稳定性和临床获益上的比较数据不足，仅观察到无显著供体效应，未深入分析为何选择单一供体而非混合供体。\",\n            \"PEG肠道准备的具体配方浓度、体积及服用时间未详细说明。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::25fa34eabb812f0508d3952a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The paper provides mechanistic insights linking clinical response to microbial engraftment, noting that responders and long-term survivors showed enrichment of short-chain fatty acid (SCFA)-produ taxa (e.g., Blautia, Roseburia, Faecalibacterium) and glycan-modifying enzymes. It also suggests that mild FMT-specific gastrointestinal toxicity may serve as a marker for successful microbial integration and immune priming. Additionally, the text contrasts these findings with historical RCT data (e.g., KEYNOTE-006, CheckMate 067) to contextualize the magnitude of observed benefits, though it acknowledges limitations regarding patient selection bias.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_8a825f7f53\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials. This study is a Phase I single-arm trial, not a Phase III RCT. While it mentions a planned Phase II randomized trial (ME.17), it does not provide data on any completed Phase III trials confirming efficacy.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports results from the MIMic trial, a multicenter, single-arm Phase I safety trial evaluating oral FMT combined with anti-PD1 therapy in 20 patients with advanced melanoma. The study found that the combination was safe and associated with an objective response rate (ORR) of 65%, median progression-free survival (mPFS) of 29.6 months, and median overall survival (mOS) of 52.8 months. These outcomes were compared favorably to historical randomized controlled trials (RCTs) of anti-PD1 monotherapy. The authors explicitly state that the sample size was small, there was no control arm, and the results are hypothesis-generating. The study identifies a subsequent randomized Phase II Canadian study (ME.17, NCT06623461) designed to evaluate the potential benefit of this intervention.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d9a7b270e9001642aeaeb4d7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The paper provides mechanistic insights linking clinical response to microbial engraftment, noting that responders and long-term survivors showed enrichment of short-chain fatty acid (SCFA)-produ taxa (e.g., Blautia, Roseburia, Faecalibacterium) and glycan-modifying enzymes. It also suggests that mild FMT-specific gastrointestinal toxicity may serve as a marker for successful microbial integration and immune priming. Additionally, the text contrasts these findings with historical RCT data (e.g., KEYNOTE-006, CheckMate 067) to contextualize the magnitude of observed benefits, though it acknowledges limitations regarding patient selection bias.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_8a825f7f53\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials. This study is a Phase I single-arm trial, not a Phase III RCT. While it mentions a planned Phase II randomized trial (ME.17), it does not provide data on any completed Phase III trials confirming efficacy.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study reports results from the MIMic trial, a multicenter, single-arm Phase I safety trial evaluating oral FMT combined with anti-PD1 therapy in 20 patients with advanced melanoma. The study found that the combination was safe and associated with an objective response rate (ORR) of 65%, median progression-free survival (mPFS) of 29.6 months, and median overall survival (mOS) of 52.8 months. These outcomes were compared favorably to historical randomized controlled trials (RCTs) of anti-PD1 monotherapy. The authors explicitly state that the sample size was small, there was no control arm, and the results are hypothesis-generating. The study identifies a subsequent randomized Phase II Canadian study (ME.17, NCT06623461) designed to evaluate the potential benefit of this intervention.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::838e53ce99defdb274a4f6da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::47320b778a94a3f6e1bba0ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b9018b036f8b7172a084833\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eab85e6bee9c4b2fed5a5534\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e2c9835b96f8fc6dc09ac52b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f4f27ebf49eb4765b4072a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a1803946bf15951d555dd21c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0698d1c77cb0d200e790e2f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::633e7982644fd55dc1491f2b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7401efb4116390e74b3c0d15\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c4c101d96abe914328c6abdc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5e3f0657dbc810fb682a25e8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f3675d08d336269e9d5f7b86\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1bc1f290c28d78622ffb8469\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e4fe0aec77d9cea7ccfbcb3b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bee8d56ffb923bd61271c4b9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2653a9eca08d3e9b4aabdd40\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6f7f1819fb2b6498ee2e73b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::246f46b2e4daa7c0826508a1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::01a4eaf6f9130e6df88a4449\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c302f1d1ebc15fb248ecf95b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::297962d07c0123503e761a0c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4677960f83a51b4866588b1e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::368f88790e7cd7be69d3482e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d402e4e4dd606e12c0dadf8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-0c71639dc3330990d568\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2c047b67f79872fa4042\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2d4faf2da7bc361a24e6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::782ec3f7244d0ab076658c3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science Core Collection, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the effects of gut microbiota or metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction was guided by STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: first covering ICI mechanisms, then the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, followed by specific metabolite classes, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and finally microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d7e9648a9d3a228b80acd4f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut microbes and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, categorizing interventions by their molecular targets (STING, NOD2, AhR, etc.).\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review acknowledges significant methodological heterogeneity across studies and notes that many proposed biomarkers and interventions require validation in large-scale, standardized longitudinal studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6e33ef85bc9029ac9138418\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Melanoma patients treated with anti-CTLA-4 (ipilimumab)\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (e.g., B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for antitumor efficacy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69bf00aad7ea27d8d011a5f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"NSCLC patients treated with anti-PD-1\",\n          \"finding\": \"High relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila (Akk-high) was associated with worse overall survival compared to Akk-low groups, challenging the binary 'good vs bad' bacteria concept and highlighting cohort/cancer-type dependency.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d3b8e49c5165f6a25f200eab\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent; different ICIs rely on distinct microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1 vs. Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5a2ef1b4e9581d3a710c521\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Tryptophan metabolites (3-IAld, IPA)\",\n          \"finding\": \"3-IAld alleviates colitis and enhances efficacy via AhR/IL-22; IPA provides cardioprotection via AhR/PI3K/AKT signaling.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::361feac329a052a7d78f53b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SCFAs (Butyrate, Propionate, Acetate)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Butyrate protects against cardiotoxicity via PPARa-CYP4X1 and enhances antigen presentation via HDAC inhibition; Propionate/Acetate promote Treg homeostasis and memory CD8+ T-cell differentiation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::120f673d74db8c5732a0396e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"TMAO\",\n          \"finding\": \"Triggers immunogenic tumor cell death (pyroptosis) via PERK-GSDME pathway, recruiting CD8+ T cells.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b3cf17eff823e01454721f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Probiotics (LGG, BF839, Akk)\",\n          \"finding\": \"LGG and BF839 activate cGAS-STING axis in dendritic cells to enhance CD8+ T cell infiltration; Akk produces c-di-AMP which directly activates STING.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0b0761c9932abc9ab5a5874d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT interventions\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT from long-term responders to PD-1 therapy showed higher efficacy than healthy donors; response correlated with loss of deleterious baseline species rather than just engraftment of donor strains.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6c7424e735d637988d2eced9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The clinical utility of ICIs is limited by interpatient variability in efficacy and the occurrence of systemic toxicities (irAEs). The review aims to systematically delineate the microbiome-metabolite-immune axis to understand these variations and optimize the balance between therapeutic gain and toxicity, ultimately guiding the development of precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b70d300ebe4f7a632702a5f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the gut microbiome and its metabolic byproducts as systemic regulators of immune function, specifically in the context of cancer immunotherapy using immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It covers mechanisms of ICI action (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, TIM-3), the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions across different cancer types and cohorts, microbial metabolites (tryptophan derivatives, SCFAs, TMAO, inosine, bile acids, polyamines) as mediators of efficacy and toxicity, and microbiome-based interventions including probiotics, FMT, postbiotics, and dietary fiber.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e3b528b07174c7f2c4e9b9b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and microbe-derived metabolites regulate the efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) of ICIs. It highlights specific taxa like Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, and Akkermansia muciniphila that potentiate therapeutic responses via pathways such as cGAS-STING and NOD2. The review also details how microbial metabolites protect organs like the heart and colon from inflammation while enhancing anti-tumor immunity. It evaluates emerging interventions like FMT and next-generation probiotics, noting that while preclinical and Phase I trials show feasibility, substantial hurdles remain regarding cohort heterogeneity, methodological standardization, and the need for large-scale longitudinal studies to establish reproducible predictive models.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7a16470a938828a019a65473\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critiques the reliance on single-taxa abundance, advocates for topology-based approaches, and highlights logistical barriers like metagenomic turnaround times for precision nutrition.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf0ea10d71d03a741315fcbb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Describes FMT from responders vs. healthy donors, encapsulation technologies for probiotics, and the double-edged nature of antibiotic preconditioning and high-fiber diets.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cebf65ae6c2fb3a2b3291c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Findings are based on a synthesis of various studies with differing methodologies; causal relationships are often inferred from preclinical models or observational data rather than definitive clinical trials.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details the context-dependent nature of microbiome-ICI interactions, showing that beneficial taxa vary by cancer type and ICI regimen (e.g., Bacteroides for CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium for PD-1, variable role of Akk). It also discusses the trade-off between efficacy and toxicity, noting that some microbes protective in one context may be detrimental in another.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2d90e74ef12c1e1106eacf6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are described from murine models or in vitro studies; human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are noted as undefined.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides specific molecular mechanisms linking microbes/metabolites to immune modulation. For example, it describes how LGG and BF839 activate the cGAS-STING pathway, how tryptophan metabolites act via AhR, and how SCFAs influence T-cell function and barrier integrity through epigenetic and receptor-mediated pathways.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::74ec76742b9f6daf3762643e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide quantitative meta-analytic results; effect sizes and statistical significance should not be inferred from this text alone.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::995110f30544c2be6aece91c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models (mice) or small clinical cohorts; extrapolation to broader human populations requires caution.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b16eb73c69f940a7edbd13bf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The role of specific microbes (e.g., Akkermansia) can be context-dependent and even contradictory across studies; avoid treating any single taxon as universally beneficial or detrimental.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d7b3fab2b1cb1884ae2d02d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Claims about the efficacy of interventions like FMT or probiotics are primarily based on early-phase trials or preclinical data; robust clinical validation is still needed.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de02bcabb5761d1a2aab77da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"approach\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n            \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n                \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"key_findings\": [\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n                \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n                \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n                \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n            \"problem_or_question\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n            \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n            \"work_summary\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1431bb03ae021761d8f92368\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"broader_review_uses\": [\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Sets the stage for why microbiome modulation is a critical area of research in overcoming ICI limitations.\",\n                \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Contextual background on ICI mechanisms and limitations\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Provides evidence on the feasibility and challenges of translating microbiome science into clinical practice, highlighting the gap between preclinical success and clinical implementation.\",\n                \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Evaluation of microbiome-based interventions\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Offers a critical perspective on the current state of the field, suggesting areas where future research needs to improve reproducibility and causal inference.\",\n                \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Methodological considerations and future directions\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"facet_contributions\": [\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to support arguments about the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions and the lack of a universal 'good' microbiome signature. Provides specific examples of taxa to discuss in the context of patient stratification.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Provides mechanistic depth for explaining how the gut microbiome influences ICI efficacy and toxicity. Useful for discussing specific signaling pathways (STING, NOD2, AhR, NF-κB) and their role in remodeling the tumor microenvironment and protecting distal organs.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n              \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n              \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n              \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bd2a31924b2f1b7a5c0db505\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2088384ebad86f83dd115cc2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::182a456925359bd5e4cb6b24\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"local_passages\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"external_calls\": 0,\n          \"passages\": [\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"机制\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\",\n                \"mechanisms mediate effect\",\n                \"ici\",\n                \"i\",\n                \"ii\",\n                \"iii\",\n                \"nsclc\",\n                \"rct\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 120.720283,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"Supplementary question reading\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"directed_content\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"{\\\"auxiliary_material\\\": \\\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": [], \\\"gap_id\\\": \\\"case_E_phase3_rct\\\", \\\"judgment_path\\\": \\\"F:\\\\\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\\\\\outputs\\\\\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\\\\\03_external_closure\\\\\\\\runs\\\\\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\\\\\source_units\\\\\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\\\", \\\"limitations\\\": [], \\\"material_ready\\\": true, \\\"material_usefulness\\\": \\\"suppor…\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 17.613751,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"general understanding\",\n                \"work summary\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"card_work_summary\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. m, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"question\": \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\n          \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::297360b98d6705da27fdef6c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e3a4f29ae0327075e8a0f972\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0eee6b0fc85c1aa61c7d0f69\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙述性综述方法。电子数据库搜索策略包括关键词“cancer”、“immunotherapy/immune checkpoint inhibitor”和“microbiome/microbiota”。纳入标准限定为：成人（>18岁）、英文全文、同行评审期刊发表的研究。排除动物模型研究以专注于临床应用证据。对纳入的10项研究进行定性综合，按癌症类型（黑色素瘤、HCC、NSCLC等）和治疗结果（疗效、irAEs、FMT干预）分类整理发现。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f0e5381ebc2cc88f3e2bff9f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"首次专门针对临床研究的综述，汇总了肠道微生物组作为ICIs疗效预测生物标志物和irAEs风险因子的证据，强调了FMT在逆转耐药性方面的初步临床可行性。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所纳入的研究样本量普遍较小（多数n≤42），存在异质性（不同癌症类型、不同ICI药物、不同测序方法如16S rRNA与宏基因组）。观察性研究无法确立因果关系。未对纳入的非随机研究进行严格的质量偏倚风险评估。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cd1eb32400edde04370e97c2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"接受ICIs治疗的晚期癌症患者（黑色素瘤、HCC、NSCLC等）\",\n          \"finding\": \"基线肠道微生物组的多样性和组成与ICIs疗效显著相关。高α-多样性通常与较长的PFS和OS相关。特定菌属富集与响应正相关（如Fecalibacterium prausnitzii, Bifidobacterium longum, Akkermansia muciniphila），而某些拟杆菌目（Bacteroidales）丰度高则与非响应相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5d7e1fba79b4eaef4b2e294\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"接受CTLA-4抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者\",\n          \"finding\": \"低丰度的Bacteroidetes门细菌与免疫检查点抑制剂诱导的结肠炎（GI毒性）相关；相反，较高的Bacteroidetes丰度与抵抗结肠炎发生相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::10fa00141f5ccb618952ade4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"抗PD-1难治性转移性黑色素瘤患者接受来自响应者的FMT\",\n          \"finding\": \"两项突破性临床试验显示，将来自免疫治疗响应者的粪菌移植给难治性患者，结合抗PD-1治疗，可使部分患者重新获得临床响应（Baruch et al. 3/10响应；Davar et al. 6/15响应），且安全性良好。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::322e6c1f1dc5e420331aed00\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3e9b4c255e7f49de211bb37f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管免疫疗法提高了部分晚期癌症患者的生存率，但仅少数患者受益且常伴随严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。目前尚缺乏基于临床证据的指导方针来利用肠道微生物组预测治疗反应或管理副作用。本研究试图厘清肠道微生物组作为预测生物标志物的潜力及其在增强疗效和减少副作用中的作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::da974f2fb7161247d30ad326\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"临床癌症患者（晚期转移性黑色素瘤、肝细胞癌、非小细胞肺癌及肾细胞癌），聚焦于免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）治疗前后的肠道微生物组特征及其与疗效和不良事件的关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::39e920e15e0d4141f1858275\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述旨在评估肠道微生物组对癌症患者免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）临床结局及相关不良事件（AEs）的影响。作者检索了截至2021年3月的PubMed、Medline和ScienceDirect数据库，筛选出10项涉及成年人的临床研究。研究综合分析了基线微生物组的多样性（α/β多样性）和组成成分与ICIs疗效（无进展生存期PFS、总生存期OS）及胃肠道毒性（如结肠炎）之间的关联，并探讨了粪菌移植（FMT）在难治性患者中的潜在调节作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0539b1b2c53b3d7b72cb824c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些关联主要基于观察性研究，存在癌症类型异质性和样本量小的限制，不能直接推断因果机制。不同研究中具体差异菌种存在不一致性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了多项临床研究数据，表明基线肠道微生物组的特定组成（如Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Bifidobacterium longum, Akkermansia muciniphila的高丰度）和较高多样性与ICIs治疗的良好临床响应（延长PFS/OS）相关。同时指出Bacteroidales的高丰度与非响应相关。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::080e444842a4a14c522c5a13\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅两项研究涉及此方面，且主要针对CTLA-4抑制剂，推广至其他ICI需谨慎。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了肠道微生物组与免疫治疗不良反应（特别是结肠炎）的联系。低Bacteroidetes丰度与CTLA-4诱导的结肠炎风险增加相关。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0fc5763ac32ca8ee7111a467\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"样本量极小，仅为概念验证性质。供体和受体间的个体差异、预处理抗生素的使用等因素可能影响结果。尚未阐明具体的分子机制或关键菌株。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"通过FMT临床试验（Baruch et al., Davar et al.）展示了从响应者向难治者移植微生物组可恢复部分患者的治疗响应，并观察到CD8+ T细胞激活增加和IL-8表达髓系细胞减少。这为微生物组介导免疫治疗效应的因果假设提供了最强的临床间接证据。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0151b710263ede70d23b60e6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"主要是相关性观察，未详细区分抗生素种类、使用时机及具体影响的�